PLACEHOLDER — choose a license before public release.

Recommended candidates for a protocol + reference implementation of this
shape:

  - Apache License 2.0      — permissive; explicit patent grant; standard
                              for protocol projects.
  - MIT License             — most permissive; no patent grant.
  - BSD 3-Clause            — permissive; explicit no-endorsement clause.
  - MPL 2.0                 — file-level weak copyleft; useful when you
                              want modifications to one file to remain
                              open without copyleft propagating.
  - AGPL 3.0                — strong copyleft including network use;
                              chooses to make hosted forks open.

Considerations specific to Origin:

  - The protocol document (protocol/origin-protocol-v0.md) and the test
    fixtures (protocol/v0-fixtures/) benefit from a permissive license
    so other implementations can be built freely against them.
  - The reference implementation in this repository can carry the same
    license or a different one; Apache 2.0 is the safest default for
    "we want this protocol to be widely implemented."

To activate this file, replace its contents with the full text of the
chosen license. The repository README and CONTRIBUTING references will
pick up automatically once this file is populated.
